.TH OMNIC 1 "2026-11-05" "omnic 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
omnic \- universal compressor with automatic codec selection and .omnic archives
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omnic
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.IR file ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B omnic
compresses and decompresses files across 16 formats. On compression it
samples the file (4 MiB entropy estimate), classifies it (extension
first, entropy fallback), and looks up a compiled-in policy table to
pick codec and level for the requested profile. Already-compressed and
high-entropy files are skipped by default. Decompression auto-detects
the format from magic bytes (extension as fallback) and works on
products of the official CLIs of every supported codec.
.PP
It also packs directory trees into
.B .omnic
archives: files are classified, grouped into per-codec buckets, and
compressed as 64 MiB solid blocks. Already-compressed assets are
stored as-is. A corrupted block can never take the rest of the archive
down \- extraction skips it and reports every affected file.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR c ", " compress
Compress each file. Output is
.IR file . ext
(next to the input unless
.B \-\-output\-dir
is given). The source file is removed on success unless
.B \-k
is given.
.TP
.BR d ", " decompress
Decompress each file; format is auto-detected. A
.B .omnic
archive (by magic bytes) is extracted as a whole tree.
.TP
.B pack
Pack a directory tree into a
.BR .omnic .
Default output is
.IR dir .omnic ;
refuses if the output would land inside the source tree.
.TP
.B unpack
Extract a
.B .omnic
archive. Supports selective extraction
.RB ( \-\-file ),
listing
.RB ( \-\-list )
and verification without writing
.RB ( \-\-verify ).
.TP
.B analyze
Classify files and print the decision (type, entropy, codec, level,
reason) without compressing.
.TP
.B list
List compiled-in codecs, levels, and recognized formats.
.TP
.BR version ", " help
Print version / usage.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR "\-c, \-\-codec " \fINAME\fR
Override the policy table and use codec
.IR NAME
(see
.BR list ).
.TP
.BR "\-l, \-\-level " \fIN\fR
Override the level.
.TP
.BR "\-p, \-\-profile " \fINAME\fR
One of
.BR fast_compress " (fc)," fast_decompress " (fd)," best_ratio " (br)," balanced
(bl, default).
.TP
.BR "\-T, \-\-threads " \fIN\fR
Thread hint (accepted; most codecs are single-threaded in this build).
.TP
.BR "\-o, \-\-output\-dir " \fIDIR\fR
Compressed outputs go into
.IR DIR .
For
.B pack
this is the archive path; for
.B unpack
it is the output root (same as
.BR \-C ).
.TP
.BR "\-C, \-\-dir " \fIDIR\fR
.B unpack
output root directory.
.TP
.BR "\-f, \-\-force"
Compress even when the input looks already-compressed or random.
For
.BR unpack " \-\-file ,
overwrite an existing target file.
.TP
.BR "\-k, \-\-keep"
Keep the source file.
.TP
.BR "\-q, \-\-quiet"
Suppress the per-file report line.
.TP
.BR "\-x, \-\-explain"
Print the classification and reason for the decision. With
.B pack ,
print the per-file decision lines.
.TP
.BR "\-\-per\-file"
.BR pack :
one block per file (millisecond single-file extraction, worse ratio).
.TP
.BR "\-\-no\-skip"
.BR pack :
compress already-compressed assets too, instead of storing them as-is.
.TP
.BR "\-\-block\-size " \fIN\fR
.BR pack :
solid block limit in MiB, 1..1024 (default 64).
.TP
.BR "\-\-file " \fIPATH\fR
.BR unpack :
extract only the named archive entry (repeatable; entries sharing a
block are decompressed once).
.TP
.BR "\-\-list"
.BR unpack :
list entries (name, size, block codec, block ratio) without reading
the data area.
.TP
.BR "\-\-verify"
.BR unpack :
fully decompress and check both CRC layers without writing any files.
.TP
.BR "\-V, \-\-version ", "\-h, \-\-help"
Version / usage.
.SH FORMATS
Compression (codec, extension, levels):
zstd .zst \-5..22, lz4 .lz4 0..12, xz .xz 0..9, lzma .lzma 0..9,
zlib .gz 0..9, zlib-stream .zlib 0..9, raw-deflate .zz 0..9,
zlib-ng .gz 0..9, libdeflate .gz 0..12, brotli .br 0..11,
snappy .snappy 1..2, lzfse .lzfse 0.
Decode-only: lzip .lz, lzvn .lzvn, bzip2 .bz2, compress .Z.
.PP
.B raw-deflate
carries no checksum; a corrupted stream can decode silently
(format-inherent, same as any raw inflate implementation).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; non-zero on error (bad usage, I/O failure, unrecognized
or corrupted input).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Compress with automatic selection:
.PP
.RS
.nf
omnic c notes.txt
.RE
.PP
Best ratio, show why:
.PP
.RS
.nf
omnic c \-\-profile best_ratio \-\-explain photos/
.RE
.PP
Round-trip a specific codec at a specific level:
.PP
.RS
.nf
omnic c \-c zstd \-l 19 data.bin
omnic d data.bin.zst
.RE
.PP
Pack a tree, list it, pull one file out:
.PP
.RS
.nf
omnic pack project/ \-o backup.omnic
omnic unpack backup.omnic \-\-list
omnic unpack backup.omnic \-\-file project/src/main.c \-C restore/
.RE
.PP
Check an archive after a bad download, without writing anything:
.PP
.RS
.nf
omnic unpack backup.omnic \-\-verify
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
Project README (formats, benchmarks, archive format) at
.UR https://github.com/push-rock/omnic
.UE .
